{
  "schema": 1,
  "scope": "G01 initial render controls: independent synthetic RGB8 oracles, including JPX alpha. Pagura and six baseline engines at 72 DPI, first page, white backdrop. No timing, family support, optional-build or release-parity verdict. Includes original post 2.5 subjects, matched post 2 controls, and an ordinary glyph-sized rectangle; PDF cmap selection and name fallback remain distinct. Legacy post4 cmap admission and format8 numeric-code groups have paired controls. Supplementary numeric codes are isolated from literal-byte fallback; no UTF-16 stream-decoding or family-conformance claim. CFF2 FontDICT probes use current context-specific ignored-operator semantics; preserved legacy and omitted-Top observations remain explicitly separate. Type 1 sbw controls retain complete glyph metrics while checking PDF-owned advances in ordinary and rotated text. Top, Font and Private CFF2 DICT namespaces have paired unknown-operator controls; known-operator validation is a separate remaining boundary. TTC/OTC collections retain the earlier standalone, single-face and named two-face controls unchanged. Face selection is a measured reader policy; successful rendering does not validate digital signatures or general OpenType conformance.",
